  "workedSolution": "1. The water surface is a chord $0.5 - 0.2 = 0.3$ m from the centre. Half-angle $\\alpha = \\cos^{-1}\\frac{0.3}{0.5} = 0.9273$, so the chord subtends $\\theta = 2\\alpha = 1.8546$ radians. Segment area $= \\frac{1}{2}(0.5)^2(\\theta - \\sin\\theta) = 0.125(1.8546 - 0.96) = 0.112$ m$^2$.",
